<title>JAPAN: Japan to give $122 mln loan for Colombia oil field.</title>
<headline>Japan to give $122 mln loan for Colombia oil field.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Japan said on Tuesday that it had agreed to provide a $122 million loan to Colombia's state-owned Oleoducto Central SA (OCENSA) for an oil pipeline project in the nation's largest oil field.</p>
<p>The Ex-Im Bank will provide 60 percent of the total, or $73 million. The remainder would be co-financed by seven private banks and lead-managed by the Industrial Bank of Japan.</p>
<p>In September, the Ex-Im Bank signed an agreement to provide an untied loan worth $300 million to Colombia's Empresa Colombian de Petroleos (ECOPETROL) to develop the oil field.</p>
</text>
